# cargo-fuzz output; never committed. The seed corpus IS committed (ADR 0027
# section 6 convention), so the named seeds are re-included here over the root
# `**/fuzz/corpus/` rule: they are hand-written bytes of our own (task P4-17,
# one row in `ATTRIBUTION.md`) and copies of the committed fixtures (task
# P7-10), one directory per fuzz target. Fuzzer-generated corpus entries (sha1
# names) and everything else `cargo fuzz` writes stay untracked.
!corpus/
corpus/**
!corpus/settings_json/
!corpus/settings_json/*.json
!corpus/shortcuts_map/
!corpus/shortcuts_map/*.bin
!corpus/layout_v2/
!corpus/layout_v2/*.yaml
artifacts
coverage
target
